Give each ascription of an anonymous class instance its own type

Setup treats the type Typer ascribes to an anonymous class instance as
inferred (anonascribe), and gave it capture set variables by setting the new
type of the ascription's type tree. A quote is unpickled once, and the
expansions of a macro in one unit share the trees a splice does not change:
that type tree among them. It can hold one type, so the second expansion got
the variables of the first, which belong to the first one's scope, and a
capability of the second expansion could not flow into them:

    Note that capability `postable$proxy2` cannot flow into capture set {any}
    because postable$proxy2 in method second is not visible from any in
    value request.

The type is now made for each ascription and attached to its `Typed` node,
which the expansions do not share, and the rechecker takes it from there.

Found in Soundness's obligatory, whose `request` and `notification` each
expand telekinesis's `submit` macro.

